What we're left with is a group of

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:10.200
companies that share one very specific

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:12.840
trait. They're all spending aggressively

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:15.280
on the same thing. AI. You might be

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:17.600
thinking, "That's great. AI is the

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:20.720
future. So, this all makes sense."

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:22.680
However, not so fast. For all these AI

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.640
companies to justify their current

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:27.160
valuations, they would need to make

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:29.360
around $2 trillion in revenue. To put

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:32.640
that into perspective, that's more than

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:36.120
Nvidia, Microsoft, Apple, Alphabet,

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:38.000
Amazon, and Meta combined in 2024. This

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:40.640
shows these companies at the top of the

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:42.240
S&P 500 aren't being valued based on

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:44.040
what they earn today, but on what

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.720
investors expect them to earn in the

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:48.480
future. Now, this isn't a major issue on

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:50.360
its own as it's very common for

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.960
companies to be valued on their future

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:54.440
potential. However, it is quite worrying

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:56.800
when it's all linked to one type

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:59.480
technology. These companies are all

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:01.800
essentially making the same bet that AI

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:04.000
is the future and they're financing it

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:06.360
with a ton of debt. A great example of

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:09.960
this is Sam Altman saying he's willing

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:12.240
to commit $1.4 trillion in spending for

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:15.440
AI infrastructure when his company

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:17.520
OpenAI is currently only making 13 to 20

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:20.560
billion dollars in yearly revenue. A lot

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:22.680
of this debt is also pretty hidden. As I

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.040
discussed in my last video, these

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:26.280
companies are bumping up their

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:28.600
valuations by passing money around to

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:30.760
each other. It's a whole complicated

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:32.520
mess. Long story short, it's all a

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:34.480
massive feedback loop that keeps

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:36.640
reinforcing itself. Bigger companies

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.880
attract more passive investment, which

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:41.720
pushes their prices higher, giving them

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:43.920
a bigger share of the S&P 500 and

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:46.040
therefore even more money to grow from

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:48.080
passive index fund investors just like

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:50.640
us. This is having a knock-on effect of

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.480
making a US economy look strong.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:54.840
However, data from Deutsche Bank

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:57.160
actually argues that if it wasn't for AI

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:59.360
spending right now, then we'd already be

00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:01.760
in a recession. So, what if instead of

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:03.600
prioritizing the biggest companies, we

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:06.880
could spread our money equally across

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:09.320
every company in the S&P 500? Well, we

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:12.920
actually can with something called an

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:14.760
equal weighted S&P 500 index fund. And

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:17.799
on the surface, it looks like the

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:20.120
perfect solution. Instead of having 40%

00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:23.600
concentrated in the top 10 stocks, it's

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:25.560
around 2% as every company is treated

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:27.400
equally. By investing in something like

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.480
this, there is no doubt that you're less

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:32.200
